{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>מיץ</b> — Three roots: the first אפס המץ, the second ימצו וישתו, and the third למען תמוצו." "<b>ומיץ החלב והאף</b> — The sense in each of these is: when a thing that stands in potential to emerge does so through action — like butter and blood and anger — they are called נחרים because they are seen in them. And so the sense of מיץ is even when his anger flares at any time, as it were pressing it: מיץ יוציא ריב, meaning that he will contend with people. And he wanted to say: beware of foulness, for it drags anger, and anger drags strife."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "All three examples are scriptural citations given in Hebrew; the root under discussion is מיץ."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:46.089935Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}